    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d886">

                <pb facs="0820" n="720" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg720"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">661.4116/76: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-08T18:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 8,
                                1920—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:17 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1163. Kameneff<anchor n="14" xml:id="d886-f1"/> arrived in England by destroyer
                    from Reval on Sunday last. Krassin has also reached London [after?] short stay
                    in Copenhagen.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d886-f1" n="14" xml:id="d886-f1-content">
                <p>In the British House of Commons on Aug. 9 it was stated by the Government that
                    “the Soviet delegation is composed of … Krassin … for trade negotiations; …
                    Kamenoff … for political questions arising out of trade negotiations.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
